[h1]Grind rails, chain Tony Hawk combos, and land it.[/h1]
A BMX you actually [b]ride[/b]: lean to steer, pedal up the ramps, grind any rail or ledge on any map, flip, whip and spin, and string it all into one combo. Real physics underneath, calm and planted on top. Base Garry's Mod only, nothing to mount.

[quote][b]OFFICIAL SERVER[/b]: ride it right now with other people
Open the console (~) and paste:   [b]connect gmod.naliwajka.com:27015[/b]
(Petopia, Peter Griffin's GMod server. Type [b]/vote[/b] for BMX mode.)[/quote]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]NEW IN 1.1: the big trick update[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Combos[/b]: chain air into a grind, the grind into a manual, the manual into a hop. Land it for a multiplier bonus. Bail and it is gone.
[*][b]Tailwhips, barspins and 8 style poses[/b]: no-hander, no-footer, can-can, superman, nothing, X-up, turndown, tabletop. They stack with flips: "Backflip Superman".
[*][b]Three game modes[/b]: SKATE, Trick Attack and Combo Mambo (see below).
[*][b]Replays and a clip camera[/b]: press [b]J[/b] to watch your last 30 seconds from chase, free, filmer or follow cameras. Scrub, slow-mo, rewind, save and share.
[*][b]Two more bikes[/b]: the 24-inch [b]BMX Cruiser[/b] and the 16-inch [b]Mini BMX[/b].
[*][b]Personal bests and a leaderboard[/b] you can place in the world.
[*][b]Trick camera, filmer camera, rider stances[/b] (seated, standing, attack) and an airtime / combo speedometer line.
[*][b]A settings menu[/b]: Spawn menu > Options > BMX. Every setting has a slider, tooltip and reset. Server rows are permission-locked.
[*][b]Bell, wind and water[/b]: ring with R, wind rushes past at speed, and deep water drags, splashes and throws you off.
[*][b]A trick bot[/b] that finds ramps on its own and lands every core trick. Ride with it, or play SKATE against it.
[*][b]A smoother camera[/b] that eases after turns and ramps instead of jolting, plus fixes from real riders' sessions.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]RIDING[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Lean to steer[/b], the way a real bike turns. The bike stays upright to gravity, so banks and angled ramps do not tip you over.
[*][b]Pedal up transitions[/b] and funboxes. A vert wall still needs a run-up.
[*][b]Suspension[/b] that soaks up landings. Kerbs roll up and ledges stop you instead of launching you.
[*][b]Hands-off landings[/b] line up with the slope you land on.
[*][b]Gamepad support[/b]: an analog stick (half stick, half lean) with an adjustable deadzone.
[/list]

[h2]TRICKS AND SCORING[/h2]
[table]
[tr][th]Ground[/th][th]Air[/th][th]Grinds[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Wheelie, Manual, Stoppie, Bunny Hop[/td][td]Backflip, Frontflip, Barrel Roll, 360, Tailwhip, Barspin + 8 poses[/td][td]Crank Grind (pipes and rails), Double Peg Grind (ledges and coping)[/td][/tr]
[/table]
Grinds are found [b]automatically on any map[/b], with no map setup, sparks included. Every trick gets an on-screen callout and points, and a chain becomes a combo.

[h2]GAME MODES[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]SKATE[/b] (2-8 players): HORSE on a bike. Land a trick, and everyone else has one try to match it. Miss and you get a letter. Spell SKATE and you're out.
[*][b]Trick Attack[/b] (1-8, 2 minutes): most points wins.
[*][b]Combo Mambo[/b] (1-8, 1 minute): only your single biggest combo counts.
[/list]
Start one with [b]bmx_game_start skate|attack|mambo[/b]. Others join with [b]bmx_game_join[/b].

[h2]THREE BIKES[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]BMX[/b]: the 20-inch street bike. The all-rounder.
[*][b]BMX Cruiser[/b]: 24-inch, longer and heavier, fastest at the top end.
[*][b]Mini BMX[/b]: 16-inch, short, light and twitchy, with a low top speed.
[/list]
A fully procedural bike: painted frame, real tyres, chrome pegs, a brake cable with a gyro detangler, and pedals geared to the rear wheel. The rider sits, grips and pedals, and crashes as a ragdoll of [i]their own[/i] player model (RagMod supported). 14 paint colours, or any colour you like.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]CONTROLS[/h2]
[table]
[tr][th]Key[/th][th]On the ground[/th][th]In the air[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]E[/td][td]Get on (also picks up a fallen bike)[/td][td][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]W / S[/td][td]Pedal / rear brake[/td][td]Nose down / nose up[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]A / D[/td][td]Lean to steer[/td][td]Roll[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]SPACE[/td][td]Hold and release to hop. Tap to hop off a grind.[/td][td][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Right mouse[/td][td]Weight back: wheelie / manual[/td][td]With A/D: spin[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Left mouse[/td][td]Front brake: stoppie[/td][td]With A/D: tailwhip[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]R[/td][td]Ring the bell (in a manual: barspin)[/td][td]Barspin[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]ALT + W/S/A/D/SPACE[/td][td]Style pose in a manual[/td][td]Style pose[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]SHIFT / CTRL[/td][td]Sprint / tuck[/td][td][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]K / L / J[/td][td]Next paint / cinematic camera / replay[/td][td][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Hold C + right-click bike[/td][td]Colour picker[/td][td][/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h2]FOR SERVER OWNERS[/h2]
Server-authoritative, tested headless on a real dedicated server every commit, and holds tickrate with two dozen bikes out. Every setting is in [b]Options > BMX > Server[/b], gated by the CAMI privilege "BMX - Change Server Settings" (works with ULX / SAM / ServerGuard), and saved across restarts.
[code]bmx_max_per_player N    bikes per player (0 = no limit)
bmx_scoring 0 / bmx_combos 0    scoring off / no combo bonus
bmx_games_admin_only 1  only admins start game modes
bmx_sounds 0  bmx_bell 0  bmx_water 0  bmx_crash_ragdoll 0
bmx_reset_server        everything back to defaults[/code]

[h2]PLAYER CONSOLE[/h2]
[code]bmx_spawn [stock|cruiser|mini]   spawn a bike (or Entities tab > BMX)
bmx_color <name>                 paint your bike
bmx_replay / bmx_replay_save     watch / save your last 30 s
bmx_scores                       your personal bests
bmx_report                       a block to paste into a bug report[/code]

[h2]FOR MODDERS[/h2]
Public [b]BMX_[/b] hooks (tricks landed, combos banked, crashes and more) and [b]BMX.RegisterTrick[/b] to add your own tricks. The bike is drawn in code, so it needs no models or materials.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]FOUND A BUG? HAVE AN IDEA?[/h2]
Type [b]bmx_report[/b] in the console and paste the result in the comments. I read every comment, and updates land often.
[b]Coming next:[/b] skateboards.

[i]Works in singleplayer and on servers. Base Garry's Mod only, with no content from other games. MIT licensed.[/i]
